Subject: [core] local-devnet network — fixed gas limit for public RPC endpoints

Base: lib/core @ fe5aa4956 (lidofinance/core, feat/scratch-dg)
Applies to: hardhat.config.ts

WHY
  Step 01 drives core's hardhat scratch deploy over the `local-devnet` network. Against a public
  endpoint (drpc et al.) eth_estimateGas under-estimates CALLs that CREATE contracts internally
  (Aragon ENSFactory.newENS): the tx goes out with a too-low limit and reverts OutOfGas. A fixed
  limit above any single scratch-deploy tx bypasses the bad estimate.

  Deploy-mechanics only: no bytecode or state consequence.

HISTORY
  Also carried `timeout: 600_000` until 3388091cc, where upstream added a 20-minute timeout to
  local-devnet itself — that half is now redundant and was dropped.

  Upstream also pins local-devnet's chainId to LOCAL_DEVNET_CHAIN_ID (default 32382). Step 01
  exports LOCAL_DEVNET_CHAIN_ID=11155111 for the Sepolia fork rather than patching the default.

diff --git a/hardhat.config.ts b/hardhat.config.ts
index 8af283e16..492985837 100644
--- a/hardhat.config.ts
+++ b/hardhat.config.ts
@@ -81,6 +81,11 @@ const config: HardhatUserConfig = {
       timeout: 20 * 60 * 1000, // 20 minutes
       accounts: [process.env.LOCAL_DEVNET_PK || ZERO_PK],
       chainId: parseInt(process.env.LOCAL_DEVNET_CHAIN_ID || "32382", 10),
+      // Fixed gas limit (bypass eth_estimateGas). Some public endpoints (drpc) under-estimate
+      // CALLs that CREATE contracts internally (e.g. Aragon ENSFactory.newENS) → the tx is sent
+      // with a too-low limit and reverts OutOfGas. A fixed high limit (well above any single Lido
+      // scratch-deploy tx, comfortably under Sepolia's block gas limit) avoids the bad estimate.
+      gas: 20_000_000,
     },
     // testnets — long RPC timeout to survive occasional Infura/Alchemy
     // headers stalls during long scratch deploys.
